 ## Overview
-This method performs 3D inpainting of Neural Radiance Fields (NeRFs) by substituting a single reference view with a diffusion-generated target view, then optimizing the NeRF to match the new view while maintaining consistency with the remaining input views. It solves the problem of inserting or modifying objects in a 3D scene without requiring multi-view supervision for the target content. It differs from [Inpainting SDS Loss](11185-inpainting-sds-loss.md) by using a deterministic 2D inpainting prior (Stable Diffusion) followed by a bilateral solver for residual smoothing, rather than relying solely on gradient-based SDS guidance during optimization.
+This method performs 3D inpainting of Neural Radiance Fields (NeRFs) by substituting a single reference view with a diffusion-generated target view, then optimizing the NeRF to match the new view while maintaining consistency with the remaining input views [S1]. It solves the problem of inserting or modifying objects in a 3D scene without requiring multi-view supervision for the target content [S1]. It differs from [Inpainting SDS Loss](11185-inpainting-sds-loss.md) by using a deterministic 2D inpainting prior (Stable Diffusion) followed by a bilateral solver for residual smoothing, rather than relying solely on gradient-based SDS guidance during optimization [S1].
 
 ## How it works
